The root cause is now concrete: this sandbox reports process PID `2`, but its mounted `/proc` has no `/proc/2/exe`; Lean 4.22 resolves its executable via `/proc/<getpid>/exe`, so both Lean and Lake lose their installation path. I’m applying a narrowly scoped runtime shim that redirects only `/proc/<digits>/exe` readlink calls to `/proc/self/exe`. This repairs the sandbox namespace mismatch without changing any frozen or generated input, and I’ll rerun the unmodified trusted checker afterward.
